Z||000004||batboy||02-29-2000||04:32 PM||||Sluppy, I ordered mine from F.O.C.O.A. and it's supposed to be like the one you have on your silver Fiero, except without the driving light cut-outs. I always liked that style of air dam, looks good on the pointy nosed Fieros in my opinion.<P>Well, I just ordered a pair of those Trans Am hood louvers from Pontiac. The local parts store ordered me a pair of Grabriel Gas Ryder front shocks to match my rear coil-over strut cartridges. I'm going to order the dew strips soon. Actually, that needs done on my 85 GT too.<P>I guy at work has a nice 95 Monte Carlo and I really like the wing on it. Here is an aftermarket replacement wing available for it. Let me know what everyone thinks. I like the clean aerodynamics and the third brake light built in. I know some people will think it sucks. But, I'm wanting something a little different fromt the standard run of the mill Fiero wing.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.jegs.com/photos/0102734.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||02-29-2000||08:25 PM||||I like it! I think it will look sweet as long as it doesn't stop too short at each end of the deck lid. I think any more than 6 to 8 inches from reaching each end wouldn't look right. Is it long enough?||||reg||14
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||02-29-2000||08:40 PM||||I'm with it Batboy, & gokart has a good point about being long enough. I like a little different style also  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and not to high. That looks like it would work. Go for it!||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||02-29-2000||08:45 PM||||The Monte Carlo wing is a little shorter by a few inches (not sure how much). That wing in the pic (Monte Thruster) is more agressive and taller than the factory Monte wing. I'll measure both wings tomorrow (95 Monte Carlo and my 85 Fiero GT). A couple times we have been parked side-by-side at work and I thought the wing looked good when I tried to imagine it on my car.||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||03-01-2000||04:30 PM||||The Monte Carlo wing is about 6 inches shorter and narrower too. It will be about 1-2 inches shorter than the length of the Fiero deck lid. I may have to think on this idea some more. It might be a bit too short for my liking.||||reg||1
